  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the Promenade des Anglais, between the Hôtel Negresco and the Palais de la Méditerranée, Le Temps d'un Été combines a private pebble beach and a beach restaurant, at 25 promenade des Anglais, opposite the Hôtel Westminster. The restaurant serves creative summer cuisine with Mediterranean touches, with fresh fish, selected meats, an oyster bar, freshly made salads and seasonal desserts. It holds the Qualité Tourisme and Clef Verte labels. The beach offers sunbed, parasol and towel hire, showers and changing rooms; the restaurant is open to you without hiring a sunbed.</p>

      <h2>Good to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office and regional tourism board pages, read on 15/11/2026, state "Animals are not accepted" for the restaurant. The establishment's website gives no rule about dogs: with no official source saying otherwise, this page keeps the refusal. To ask for an exception, call 04 83 66 02 49. The website announces opening every day from 10am to 7pm; the Nice tourist office says open all year, every day.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: plan another table for you and your dog, or a dog beach (see below).</div>

      <h2>Where to go with your dog nearby</h2>
      <p>The City of Nice lists two beaches open to dogs all year: La Lanterne beach, in the west of Nice (400 promenade des Anglais, behind the Carras harbour), and Lenval beach, in the middle of the Promenade des Anglais, at numbers 137 to 147, marked in summer by two statues and barriers (municipal orders 2008-00481 and 2010-2049, article 26).</p>
    </div>

